SEG = 'ROL'
CAT = 'hhaRole'
Q = [
('Who prepares the written care instructions a home health aide follows?',
 'RN or assigning therapist', ["The patient's physician", 'Agency office scheduler', 'Previous aide on the case'],
 "42 CFR 484.80(g)(1): the registered nurse or other skilled professional (PT, OT or speech therapist) who assigns the aide writes the patient care instructions. The physician orders the plan of care but does not write the aide's instructions."),
('Under 42 CFR 484.80, aides may assist with which medications?',
 'Ones usually self-administered', ['Any medication taken by mouth', 'Ones the family has approved', 'Over-the-counter medicines only'],
 'The federal duties list allows "assistance in administering medications ordinarily self-administered." It is not limited to over-the-counter drugs, and the family cannot widen it.'),
('A patient asks to borrow $20 from her aide until payday. What does the aide do?',
 'Kindly say no', ['Lend it and tell the nurse', 'Lend it with a written IOU', 'Give it as a small gift'],
 "Lending money mixes the aide into the patient's finances and crosses a professional boundary. The aide declines kindly and can let the nurse know if money is short."),
('A patient refuses her bath today. What does the aide do?',
 'Accept it, then tell the RN', ['Bathe her quickly and gently', 'Skip it and tell no one', 'Have her son persuade her'],
 '42 CFR 484.50(c)(4) gives patients the right to refuse care. The aide accepts the refusal, records it and tells the nurse so the plan can be reviewed.'),
('Which right does 42 CFR 484.50 give every home health patient?',
 'To refuse care', ['To unlimited aide visits', 'To services outside the plan', 'To keep the aide after discharge'],
 'Patients may participate in, consent to or refuse care before and during treatment. Visit frequency and services come from the plan of care, not unlimited choice.'),
("A patient's son asks the aide for his mother's diagnosis. She has not agreed to share it. Best reply?",
 'Refer him to her or the nurse', ['Tell him, since he is her son', 'Show him her plan of care', 'Tell him the main diagnosis only'],
 '42 CFR 484.50(c)(6) gives the patient a confidential clinical record. Being family does not entitle the son to it without her agreement.'),
("An aide sees new grip-shaped bruises on a patient's upper arms. What must the aide do?",
 'Report it to the agency now', ['Note it and watch for more', 'Report it at the next visit', 'Ask the family how it happened'],
 '42 CFR 484.50(e)(2): staff who notice possible abuse or injuries of unknown source must report them immediately to the HHA and, per state law, other authorities. Waiting or questioning the family first delays protection.'),
("A caregiver takes cash from the patient's purse without asking. This is:",
 'Misappropriation', ['Neglect of care', 'Verbal abuse', 'A family matter'],
 "Taking a patient's money or belongings without permission is misappropriation of property, which 42 CFR 484.50 protects patients from even when a relative does it."),
('A caregiver threatens to leave a patient alone unless she eats. This is:',
 'Mental abuse', ['Neglect', 'Physical abuse', 'Misappropriation'],
 'Threats that cause fear are mental abuse. Neglect is failing to give needed care, and physical abuse involves bodily harm.'),
('How much in-service training must a home health aide complete?',
 '12 hours each 12 months', ['8 hours each 12 months', '12 hours every 2 years', '24 hours each 12 months'],
 '42 CFR 484.80(d) requires at least 12 hours of in-service training during each 12-month period, supervised by a registered nurse.'),
('After how long without paid aide work must an aide complete a new program?',
 '24 consecutive months', ['12 consecutive months', '36 consecutive months', '6 consecutive months'],
 '42 CFR 484.80(a)(2): a continuous 24-month period without furnishing services for pay means the aide must complete another training or competency program.'),
("For a patient also receiving skilled nursing, how often does the RN assess the aide's services?",
 'At least every 14 days', ['At least every 30 days', 'At least every 60 days', 'At least once a year'],
 '42 CFR 484.80(h)(1) requires a supervisory assessment no less than every 14 days for patients receiving skilled services. Every 60 days applies to aide-only patients.'),
("For an aide-only patient, how often must the RN visit to check the aide's services?",
 'Every 60 days', ['Every 14 days', 'Every 30 days', 'Every 90 days'],
 '42 CFR 484.80(h)(2): when no skilled service is given, the RN makes an onsite visit every 60 days. The 14-day rule is for patients with skilled care.'),
('An aide was rated unsatisfactory on catheter care. Until retrained and retested, she may do it:',
 'Under direct RN supervision', ['After reading agency policy', 'If the patient agrees to it', 'With a family member watching'],
 '42 CFR 484.80(c)(4): an aide may not perform a task rated unsatisfactory without direct RN supervision until she is retrained and passes a new evaluation.'),
('Which task is within the home health aide role?',
 'Assisting with walking', ['Packing a deep wound', 'Setting a feeding pump', 'Giving a flu shot'],
 'The duties in 42 CFR 484.80(g)(3) include personal care, simple procedures as an extension of therapy or nursing, and help with walking or exercises. Wound packing, pump settings and injections are licensed tasks.'),
("A patient asks the aide to drive her to a friend's party. Outings aren't on the care plan. What does the aide do?",
 'Check with the supervisor', ['Drive her, since it lifts her mood', 'Take her by taxi instead', 'Go if her family agrees'],
 'Aides provide services that are in the plan of care. A task outside it needs the supervisor first, both for the plan and for agency liability.'),
('The plan lists a daily sponge bath. The patient wants it after breakfast, not before. What does the aide do?',
 'Give it after breakfast', ['Call the nurse to approve', 'Give it before, as listed', 'Skip it today'],
 "The timing within the visit is the patient's choice and the bath is still given as planned. No approval is needed for honoring a reasonable preference."),
('The plan says to walk the patient to the porch twice daily. She feels well and asks to go. What does the aide do?',
 'Walk with her as planned', ["Get the nurse's OK first", 'Let her go alone', 'Wait for the therapist'],
 'Walking is on the plan and she is well, so the aide simply does the assigned task. Calling first adds nothing, and letting her go alone ignores the plan.'),
("A doctor phones the patient's home and gives the aide a new medication order. What does the aide do?",
 'Ask him to call the RN', ['Write it in the visit note', 'Start the new dose today', 'Tell the patient to follow it'],
 '42 CFR 484.60(b)(3): verbal orders may be taken only by staff authorized by state law and agency policy, which does not include aides. The nurse takes and records the order.'),
('A patient with little English needs to understand a change in care. What must the agency provide?',
 'Free language services', ['Interpreting by a grandchild', 'Notice in English only', 'An interpreter at her cost'],
 '42 CFR 484.50(f)(2) requires language services, including interpreting and translation, at no cost to patients with limited English.'),
('A patient complains to her aide that a nurse was rude. Under 42 CFR 484.50, she has the right to:',
 'Complain without reprisal', ['Have that nurse fired at once', 'Stop visits for a month', 'Complain in writing only'],
 'Patients may make complaints to the HHA and must be free from discrimination or reprisal for voicing grievances. The agency must investigate and document it.'),
("A patient's daughter asks the aide to give her mother an extra pain pill tonight. What does the aide do?",
 'Refer the request to the RN', ['Give it if the label allows', 'Give it if pain is severe', 'Leave the pill out for the daughter'],
 'Drugs are given only as ordered (42 CFR 484.60(b)(1)) and aides only assist with self-administered medications. Any dose change goes through the nurse and prescriber.'),
("Who must aides report changes in a patient's condition to?",
 'RN or skilled professional', ["The patient's physician directly", 'The family caregiver', 'The next aide on the case'],
 '42 CFR 484.80(g)(4): aides are members of the interdisciplinary team and must report changes in condition to a registered nurse or other appropriate skilled professional.'),
('A patient asks the aide to witness and sign her new will. What does the aide do?',
 'Decline and tell the agency', ['Sign as a witness only', 'Sign it if a notary is present', 'Sign if her family agrees'],
 'Signing legal papers for a patient mixes the aide into her personal affairs and can lead to claims of undue influence. Aides decline and let the agency guide the patient.'),
]
